Scion: VMAPPLE without Apple's hypervisor -- architectural PAC keys (SCION_NATIVE_PAC).

Modifications to Apple's xnu (xnu-12377.121.6), Apple Public Source License 2.0
(APSL-2.0); see https://www.opensource.apple.com/apsl/. Copyright of the original
files: Apple Inc. These changes: Scion contributors. Design after UniXNU's
native-pac-keys.patch (BSD-2-Clause-Patent); no UniXNU code is copied.

Build with `make ... MACHINE_CONFIGS=VMAPPLE SCION_NATIVE_PAC=1`; without the switch
the kernel is unchanged. With it, HAS_PARAVIRTUALIZED_PAC is not defined, so no
VMAPPLE_PAC_* hvc is made; PAC_INIT_KEY_STATE fills one key set per boot and
loads it into APIA/APIB/APDA/APDB/APGA on every CPU before SCTLR_EL1 enables the
keys. EL0 and EL1 share that set (no per-process keys), which is weaker than
Apple's model: see docs/AVF-VMAPPLE.md section 4.

